### Key Commands Summary:
```bash
# Repository setup
gh repo clone Vishuu77/Machine-Learning-Data-Science-Projects- gh_restructure

# File organization
mkdir -p Flight_Price_Prediction/model PAN_Card_Tampering_Detection Dog_Breed_Prediction/model
git mv flight_app.py train_model.py Data_Train.xlsx Test_set.xlsx Flight_Price_Prediction/
git mv pan_app.py PAN_Card_Tampering_Detection/
git mv dog_app.py train_dog_model.py Dog_Breed_Prediction/

# Path corrections
patch Flight_Price_Prediction/flight_app.py # Replace hardcoded paths
patch Flight_Price_Prediction/train_model.py # Replace hardcoded paths

# Git operations
git config user.email "vr4127806@gmail.com"
git config user.name "vishuu77"
git add .
git commit -m "Restructure: 9 clean project folders"
gh repo sync

# Space management
mkdir -p /d/ML_Projects/
cp -r /c/Users/Admin/course_projects/04_plant_disease /d/ML_Projects/
```

This complete workflow can be replicated for any data science portfolio project organization.